    "content": "The tax extension deadline to file 2025 federal income taxes in 2026 is October 15, 2026. To get this automatic six-month extension, you must file Form 4868 by the regular deadline of April 15, 2026. Note that this is an extension to file (submit paperwork), not an extension to pay any taxes owed. Form 4868 Key Details Regarding 2026 Tax Extensions: Payment Deadline: Any taxes owed must still be paid by April 15, 2026, to avoid interest and penalties. How to Apply: File Form 4868 by April 15, 2026, which can be done electronically via IRS Free File or using software. IRS Free File Business Extensions: S-Corps and partnerships generally must file extensions by March 16, 2026, while others may differ. Synonyms: Often referred to as \"automatic six-month extension,\" \"filing for more time,\" or \"postponement of time to file.\" State Extensions: Some states automatically apply the federal extension, while others require a separate state-specific form. If you are in a federally declared disaster area, you may have different, later deadlines.",
